/* lrg-shader-graph.c
 *
 * Copyright 2026 Zach Podbielniak
 *
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
 *
 * LrgShaderGraph: node graph -> fragment GLSL -> LrgShaderAsset.
 *
 * The node library is a static table (NodeDef): ports with types and
 * the default an unconnected input takes, an expression template with
 * {0}, {1}... standing for the converted inputs, whether the node is
 * computed into a temporary or inlined, and per output a swizzle suffix
 * applied to the node's value.  Most nodes are generated by that one
 * generic path; parameters, constants, swizzles, splits and the two
 * output nodes have small special cases.
 *
 * Types: ports are float/vec2/vec3/vec4/sampler2D or "dynamic".  A
 * node's dynamic ports share one resolved width, the widest source
 * feeding any of them.  A link converts float -> vecN by splatting and
 * vecN -> vecM (N > M) by truncating; anything else is a mismatch.
 *
 * Validation runs Kahn's algorithm over all nodes (nodes left over are
 * on cycles), resolves types in that topological order and collects
 * every problem with its node id.  Generation walks back from the
 * output node depth-first in port order and emits each node once, so
 * the text only depends on the graph's structure.
 */

